From e839258f889a11e03aeac265e53b41291c2a5292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] custom pads: parse_config.py support, label procs, frame
 clean-up

For pad types in config.txt that scripts/setup_custom.sh imports from a
slot submodule.  Without this, parse_config.py prints 'Bad pad type' and
exits 0:  no core signals for the slot, unsubstituted PAD_<s>_<p>_SIGNALS
in verilog/gl/sg13cmos5l_padframe.v, and the previous slot's last label
line repeated in scripts/gen_padframe.tcl.

- scripts/parse_config.py:  CUSTOM_PADS (cell -> core-side pins, in order
  along the pad's core edge) from the slot's pads/pads.txt, checked
  against the ports of magic/custom_io/<cell>.mag;  used in the four
  places that switch on the pad type.  Each pin becomes one core signal
  <signal name>_<pin>.
- scripts/custom_io_manifest.py (new):  reads the manifests.
- scripts/custom_io.tcl (new):  label_right_custom / label_left_custom:
  Via2 on the pad's M2 pin stub, 0.29 um Metal3 strap into the core,
  port label;  sourced by gen_padframe_template.tcl.
- scripts/run_update_frame_custom_io.sh (new), make frame-custom-io:
  erases the hand-made pad-edge copies of the replaced foundry pads in
  chipalooza_frame.mag (else the slot wrapper keeps the old pins too, as
  slot 6 does now);  run after make padframe, before make wrappers.
- scripts/custom_io_verilog.py (new):  prints the hand edits of the
  chip-core Verilog for slots whose pads are all custom.

Tested with slot 7 (tatzelbrumm/sg13cmos5l_cm_slot7 main 454da6a):  fork
tatzelbrumm/sg13cmos5l_ocd_chipalooza, branch claude/slot7-v2-harness-test.

